            <ArticleTitle>Regional hip blockade. A simplified technique for the relief of intractable osteoarthritic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1060-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A regional anaesthetic technique is described using a blind anatomical approach to the obturator nerve and nerve to quadratus femoris, as a means of alleviating the disabling pain of chronic osteoarthritis of the hip, when arthroplasty is not available.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
